Z||000000||Billy W||03-12-2001||10:43 AM||||Does anyone know of any engine that can replace the stock fiero engine without a $3000 V8 conversion?  I'm looking for an engine that is actually more powerful than the stock engine!  Would something Japanese work? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-12-2001||10:51 AM||||Oh yes, there is a load of info about a bunch of common engine swaps.  Most guys here wont go with jap engines, mostly because I dont think they will bolt up to the tranny well.<P>Do a search on "3.1 engine swaps"  or 3.4 TDC, 3800, 4.9 caddy.<P>More info than you would want to know.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||c m west||03-12-2001||11:15 AM||||We are devoted to swaps that you are looking for - rebuilt 2.8, 3.1, 3.4, 3.4 twin dual cam, 3.8 Series I, 3.8 Series II - both Naturally aspirated and supercharged, also we over turbocharger arrangements for any one of these motors - check out our website<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<BR>||||reg||1
